From 04889f001ca7d25e17bf0f12cfa39effc347e0ba Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Craig Johnson <1545411+captainpacket@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 18 Jul 2026 08:19:48 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 8/9] plugin: idempotent same-node wiring via
 koko.EnsureVethWire; rollback
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Same-node fabric links were realized by check-then-create: two
IsExistLinkInNS probes chose between do-nothing / remove-then-create /
skip-or-priority-gated MakeVeth. This was broken twice over. First,
IsExistLinkInNS always returned false (fixed in the koko series), so every
branch except 'neither exists' was dead and any link that actually existed
was blindly re-created — a fatal 'failed to rename link kokoNNN -> ethN:
file exists' for the WHOLE multi-link ADD. Second, even with working
probes the sequence is a TOCTOU race against the peer pod's concurrent ADD
wiring the same link from the other direction (MakeVeth creates BOTH ends,
including into our netns). On a hub pod this produced permanent
sandbox-creation retry loops: each kubelet retry re-ran a full ADD, the
peer's churning ADD re-planted the interface into each fresh netns, and
the collision recurred every ~3s.

Replace the branch soup with koko.EnsureVethWire under the symmetric
per-link alias: adopt a correct existing wire no matter which side created
it, replace stale halves, fail loudly on foreign ownership — serialized
node-wide inside koko, so both sides may attempt the same link safely. The
IsSkipped/higher-priority gate is no longer needed on the alive path (both
sides ensuring is now benign); Skip bookkeeping remains for the
peer-not-alive path.

A failed ADD now unwinds: only the local-namespace ends this invocation
realized are recorded (removing one veth end removes the pair; peer
namespaces are never touched directly in rollback), and protectedIfName
guards eth0/lo/empty names in every removal path as defense in depth.

Upstreamable together with the koko series.
